    "head_branch": "fix/metrics-archive-old-runs",
    "head_commit_message": "fix(ci): metrics-archive keeps the first sim-checks runs and survives a dropped download\n\nThe first archive run stopped at a cut-off log download (IncompleteRead),\nand `| tee` hid the failure, so it showed green. It also kept nothing for\nthe sim-checks runs of 2026-10-14 and 15, which ran everything in one job\nnamed `sim-checks`, and wrote empty .log files where the digest and\nscaling jobs were skipped.\n\n- Each read is retried (2, 4, 8 s); a download that still fails leaves\n  its run out, names it and exits 1, and a later run takes it.\n- The step runs with pipefail; the push step runs unless cancelled, so a\n  partial archive is still pushed while the run shows red.\n- A job whose name isn't kept keeps its kept steps' sections, matched to\n  the steps that ran in turn, or its whole log where they don't match.\n- Nothing to keep: {\"na\": \"not-applicable\"} and no .log; a skipped job's\n  runner image is not-applicable too.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011AyPi27hiWYpRQB4fhW5kr",
